course: dictionary
lesson: 15719
title: Words for people at work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which meaning is meant. «Tradesman» is one of these words. Read the clues around it before you decide.
explain: «The tradesman came on Monday to fix the leaking tap.» A leaking tap needs a skilled worker, so here a tradesman is someone like a plumber. Ask yourself: what job is being done? The job tells you the meaning.
explain: «Mum said, "Use the tradesman's entrance," and we went round the back to the kitchen door.» The clue is the back door. Long ago, a back door was used by deliveries and workers, so this is the older meaning: a shopkeeper or someone who delivers goods.
fact: A tradesman is a person with a skilled practical job, such as a plumber, electrician or builder.
fact: In the UK, an old meaning of «tradesman» is a shopkeeper or someone who delivers goods.
fact: «Tradesman's entrance» means a back door used for deliveries and workers.
fact: Today many people say «tradesperson» or «trades worker» to include women as well as men.
fact: The plural of tradesman is tradesmen.
exercise: «The tradesman fixed the wiring in our kitchen.» What is a tradesman here? | A pilot who flies a plane | *A skilled worker, like an electrician | A singer on the radio | A teacher who runs a school
exercise: «The servants went in by the tradesman's entrance, round the back of the big house.» What does the entrance suggest? | *A back door for deliveries and workers | A secret tunnel under the castle | The grand front door with a gold knocker | A window at the top of the tower
exercise: Which job is a tradesman most likely to do? | *Fixing a burst pipe | Teaching a maths lesson to Year 5 | Writing a novel for a library | Conducting an orchestra at a concert
test: «The tradesman arrived with his tools to mend the roof.» What do the tools and the roof tell you? | A tradesman is a child who plays in the garden | A tradesman is a king who rules the land | *A tradesman is a skilled worker who does practical jobs | A tradesman is a singer who performs on stage
test: Mia says, «Use the tradesman's entrance.» Where does she mean you should go? | The front door with the bell | The garden shed | The top of the stairs | *The back door
exam: Which word is a modern way to include everyone who does skilled practical work? | *tradesperson | shopkeeper | tradesboy | tradesmanly
